CodexBar Codex ledger mirror window: real-history proof
Verified 2026-10-05 on macOS 27.0, arm64. Counts only; dollar amounts, paths,
prompts, and account details are omitted.

Harness:
- A temporary, uncommitted Swift test in the CodexBarTests target drove the
  CLI cost path (CostUsageFetcher.loadTokenSnapshot, then renderCostText) over
  one real ~/.codex history, read-only. Each run started from its own copy of
  the same 0.72.0 cost cache (parser revision 8).
- 30-day window, America/Santiago calendar, fixed "now" of
  2026-10-05T23:00:00Z, pricing refresh off.
- Each run repeated fetch passes until the snapshot reported a full scan and
  no cached file had pending scan work. It then dumped totals and per-file row
  counts.
- main @ 6a26b2e9b and this branch ran in parallel against the same live
  history.

Results (both runs fully scanned, no pending files):

                                          main     branch
  fetch passes                             113        183
  parser revision of cached files     r8=3591    r9=3585
  ledger rows                           66,204     66,206
  legacy rows in files with ledger rows 40,807      1,714
  30-day tokens                     13,562,646,041  8,102,604,890

Per-file diff:
- No file lost ledger rows, and no file gained legacy rows.
- The branch removed 39,093 legacy rows. They are the token_count mirrors of
  ledger rows that main counted a second time.
- One live session appended 2 ledger records between the two runs, which
  accounts for 66,204 vs 66,206.
- 6 cache entries exist only in main's cache. Each has 0 rows. They are stale
  empty fragments retained from the copied cache, and the revision 9 reparse
  drops them.

Raw-log cross-check (Python, same window, read-only):
- 66,608 unique token_usage_record responses, 8.27B input and output tokens.
- 66,336 token_count events sit next to a token_usage_record with identical
  input, cached, and output tokens, within 60 s. They hold 8.21B tokens, so
  nearly every ledger response has a mirror.
- The 5.46B tokens the branch removes from main's total fit inside that mirror
  pool. Main already merged mirrors that share a timestamp or thread total.

Reproduce: add the harness as Tests/CodexBarTests/ZZMirrorRealSetupProofTests.swift
(the PR description includes its source), then run from each checkout:
  source Scripts/test_environment.sh && CODEXBAR_REAL_PROOF=1 \
    CODEXBAR_PROOF_CACHE_SOURCE=<copy of ~/Library/Caches/CodexBar> \
    CODEXBAR_PROOF_OUTPUT=<out.txt> \
    swift test --filter ZZMirrorRealSetupProofTests

Scope: one person's Codex history. It shows the duplicate rows are removed
without losing ledger rows. It does not cover forks whose parent resolves in a
later scan pass. That limit is documented in docs/codex.md.
